1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,911
Measure a voltage ten thousand times every second. In project one, your program

2
00:00:05,911 --> 00:00:10,500
waited for each measurement. At this speed it would do little else.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,280
We need help.

4
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:18,960
Meet the team. A timer is the metronome: it clicks ten thousand times a second.

5
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:23,540
The ADC is the camera: on each click, it takes one voltage snapshot.

6
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:29,552
DMA, direct memory access, is the delivery robot: it carries each snapshot to

7
00:00:29,552 --> 00:00:32,200
memory, without asking the processor.

8
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:41,109
Follow carefully. The timer tells the ADC: 'measure now'. When the ADC has a result,

9
00:00:41,109 --> 00:00:43,840
it tells DMA: 'collect this'.

10
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:50,040
A setting called cycle steal makes the robot move exactly one result per request.

11
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:54,700
Without it, the robot would race ahead and not wait for fresh measurements.

12
00:00:55,700 --> 00:01:01,220
The robot fills basket A with 64 numbers. Then it rings a doorbell.

13
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:07,778
The handler instantly points the robot at basket B, and only then tells the main

14
00:01:07,778 --> 00:01:11,640
program that A is ready. While you read A, B fills.

15
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:14,540
Then they swap. Ping, pong.

16
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,600
How long does one basket take to fill?

17
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:23,100
Your turn. Pause the video.

18
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:31,053
Sixty-four divided by ten thousand: about 6.4 milliseconds, roughly 156 baskets a

19
00:01:31,053 --> 00:01:31,740
second.

20
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:38,316
If reading takes longer than filling, a basket gets reused before you finish, or you

21
00:01:38,316 --> 00:01:38,980
skip some.

22
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:43,560
Printing is slow, so we only look at a few numbers.

23
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:50,940
With power off, a leader connects a potentiometer: outer legs to ground and 3.3

24
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:53,120
volts, middle leg to PTE30.

25
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,780
A pin left unconnected will wander.

26
00:01:56,780 --> 00:02:01,900
Metronome, camera, robot, two baskets. Let's build it.

